  "text": "Haywood County Board of Elections | Haywood County, NC\nSkip to Main Content\nCreate a Website Account\n- Manage notification subscriptions, save form progress and more.\nWebsite Sign In\nSearch\nGovernment\nServices\nResidents\nBusiness\nVisitors\nHow Do I...\nHome\nGovernment\nDepartments A - F\nElections\nHaywood County Board of Elections\nEarly voting is underway! Vote Oct 15 - 31\nLocations:\nSenior Resource Center\n(Waynesville) or\nCanton Library.\nWeekdays 8:00 AM\u20137:30 PM, Saturdays 8:00 AM\u20133:00 PM.\nEarly Voting Schedule\nExplore Early Voting and Absentee Data\n(\nupdated overnight by the North Carolina State Board of Elections\n)\nUpcoming Board of Elections Meeting Agendas: October 20 and 27\n(Absentee by Mail Review)\nVOTER TOOLS\nVoter Search\n(Check your registration, see your polling place, download a sample ballot)\nView Your Sample Ballot\n(instructions)\nEarly Voting Schedule\nElection Day Polling Place Search\nOnline\nJudicial Voter Guide: 2026 General Election\nIMPORTANT DATES\nFriday, October 9 \u2014\nVoter Registration Deadline.\nAnyone who missed the registration deadline can register and vote at early voting with certain documentation.\nLearn more:\nRegister in Person During Early Voting | NCSBE\nThursday, October 15 \u2014\nIn-person early voting began.\nSaturday, October 31 \u2014\nIn-person early voting ends.\nTuesday, October 20 \u2014\nLast day to request a no-excuse absentee ballot (5:00 PM).\nTuesday, November 3 \u2014\nElection Day. Polls open 6:30 AM\u20137:30 PM.\nVote at your assigned precinct.\nTuesday, November 3 \u2014\nLast day to return an absentee ballot (7:30 PM).\nFriday, November 13 \u2014\nCounty canvass (11:00 AM).\nPress Release:\nBulk Voter Registration Mailings Cause Voter Confusion, Additional Work for Counties | NCSBE\nPHOTO ID REQUIREMENTS\nVoters will be asked to show photo ID when voting in North Carolina. For most voters, they will simply show their driver license or state identification card. But there are many other acceptable photo IDs listed at\nVoter ID | NCSBE\n. If a voter does not have an acceptable photo ID, they may obtain a No-Fee ID at\nNCDMV\nVoter Registration\nVote By Mail\nEarly Voting\nElection Results\nCandidate Filing\nGet Involved\nAbout Us\nVoter Registration\nDownload Voter Registration Form\nto register for the first time or update your existing registration.\nYou can also register or update your existing registration online through the NCDMV at\nmyNCDMV\n. There is no fee for this service. You must have an NC Driver License or a NC ID card to use this method.\nFor more information about Registering to Vote in North Carolina, visit the\nNC State Board of Elections Website.\nVote By Mail\nHaywood County Voters must submit Absentee Request form to:\nHaywood County Board of Elections\n63 Elmwood Way, Suite A\nWaynesville, NC 28786\n(\nforms\nmay not\nbe submitted by FAX or E-mail\n)\nDownload the Absentee Request Form here:\n2026 N.C. Absentee Ballot Request Form\nIf you no longer live in Haywood County you can find your local county Elections office here\nCounty BOE Info\nMilitary & Overseas Voters\n, please refer to the\nFederal Voter Assistance Program\nMore information about voting by mail can be found at the\nNC State Board of Elections website\n.\nEarly Voting\nEarly Voting Schedule\nfor November 3, 2026 General Election\nFor more information about Early Voting in North Carolina, visit the\nNC State Board of Elections Website.\nElection Results\nCLICK HERE FOR ELECTION RESULTS\nYou will need to select the Election Date, along with any other desired filters, such as County, Office, & Contest\nCandidate Filing\nContact your local\nCounty Board of Elections Office\nfor more information. You can also visit the State Board of Elections website for more information about\nFiling for Candidacy\nand\nCampaign Finance Requirements\n.\nGet Involved\nYou can do more than just vote! Complete the online application and receive information about becoming a paid Precinct Official today.\nIt takes more than 150 paid, dedicated volunteers to operate Haywood County polling places each election.\nThese people are your friends, co-workers, and neighbors who volunteer days of paid service to ensure you can cast your ballot on Election Day.\nWe need your help, too! More Precinct Officials are needed in your neighborhood. Do your part to provide voting opportunities in your community.\nONLINE APPLICATION\nAbout Us\nAbout the Board of Elections\nEach county in North Carolina has a Board of Elections. It is a five-person bipartisan board appointed every two years by the State Board of Elections. County Board members take an oath and begin their two-year terms on the Tuesday following the third Monday in July in odd-numbered years.\nResponsibilities of the Haywood County Board of Elections\nThe Board of Elections is responsible for conducting all elections held in Haywood County. The Board administers, locally, State election laws. Principal functions include establishing Election precincts and voting sites; appointing and training precinct officials; preparing and distributing ballots and voting equipment; canvassing and certifying the ballots cast in Elections; and investigating any voting irregularities. It maintains voter registration, voting records, and provides public data on voters and Elections.\nContact Us\nRobert Inman\nDirector\nEmail Robert Inman\nDoyle Teague\nDeputy Director\nEmail Doyle Teague\nJeremy Fish\nElections Specialist\nEmail Jeremy Fish\nKristy Heatherly\nElections Specialist\nEmail Kristy Heatherly\nElections\nPhysical Address\n63 Elmwood Way\nSuite A\nWaynesville\n,\nNC\n28786\nPhone:\n828-452-6633\nQuick Links\nCheck Your Registration\nVoter Registration/ Update Form\nOnline Voter Registration\nEarly Voting Schedule\nABS by Mail Request\nView Sample Ballot\nUOCAVA Election Notice\nBoard Meeting Schedule\nVoter Search\nElection Day Polling Places\nALL\nMunicipal Election Day Polling Place\ns\nPolling Place/Precinct Search\nElection Results\nElected Officials\nVoter ID Information\nCampaign Finance\nBoard of Elections Search\nJudicial Voter Guide\nAgendas & Minutes\nApply for Jobs\nGIS Maps\nAnimal Services\nPay Taxes Online\nDevelopment Services &\nEnvironmental Health Permitting Portal\nContact Us\nHaywood County Government\n215 N Main Street\nWaynesville, NC\nMore contact info >\nMunicipalities\nTown of Waynesville\nTown of Maggie Valley\nTown of Clyde\nTown of Canton\n/QuickLinks.aspx\nQuick Links\nBid Opportunities\nBoard of Commissioners\nDeeds Online\nEmployment Opportunities\nEmployee Access\n/QuickLinks.aspx\nSite Links\nHome\nSite Map\nAccessibility\nCopyright Notices\n/QuickLinks.aspx\nGovernment Websites by\nCivicPlus\u00ae\nLoading\nLoading\nDo Not Show Again\nClose\nArrow Left\nArrow Right\n[]\nSlideshow Left Arrow\nSlideshow Right Arrow",
